# 4) Missing assets → true 404 (NOT index.html 200).
# NOTE: Netlify does NOT allow a splat in the middle of a path segment, so
# extension rules like "/*.js /404.html 404" are INVALID and silently ignored.
# Valid form: directory splats (asterisk at END of segment). The site only
# serves assets from /js/ and /og/, and the 404 catch-all in (6) covers any
# other path that is not matched above or whitelisted in (5).
/js/*     /404.html   404
/og/*     /404.html   404
# 5) Extensionless route rewrites — the ONLY paths allowed to fall through to
#     the SPA shell (index.html 200). Any extensionless path NOT matched here
#     hits the hard-404 catch-all in (6) instead of a 200 soft-404.
#     Keep this list in sync with scripts/route-whitelist.cjs —
#     scripts/check-sitemap-coverage.cjs fails the build on drift.
#     Why a whitelist: the SPA legitimately serves URLs that are NOT all
#     prerendered (runtime tool-modifier long-tails like
#     /finance/loan-emi/5-years-50000, locale-prefixed deep links /es/...
#     written by the language switcher), and Netlify splats cannot exclude
#     paths — only rule ordering can. 404-status rules respect shadowing, so
#     real files (prerendered pages, /js/*, /og/*, root assets) always win
#     even when they appear AFTER the whitelist below; the whitelist must
#     precede the 404 catch-all.
#     - 20 calculator categories (CALC_DATA keys: 7 eager + 13 lazy)
